= General Work Plan

#guide[
  *ABE Guideline:* The general work plan contains two main items: (1) a description of the research methods you will use, and (2) a time planning with specific dates. You can also demarcate your work here, indicating what you _will_ and _will not_ do.
]

== Research Methods

#guide[
  *ABE Guideline:* For each research question, explain how you will answer it. Describe:

  - How you will collect data
  - How much data you will collect and its requirements
  - Which resources you need (materials, equipment, finances)
  - Initial references for available methods in scientific literature

  *Tip:* Structure this section around your sub-questions. For each one, write a short paragraph explaining the method, the data source, and how you will analyse the results. This makes it obvious that your plan covers all the questions — and highlights any gaps early.
]

=== Methods for Sub-question 1

#guide[
  _Describe the specific method, data collection approach, tools or equipment, and analysis technique you will use to answer sub-question 1. Include references to methodological literature._
