== Scope and Demarcation

#guide[
  *Hint:* Clearly state what is _in scope_ and what is _out of scope_. This protects you from scope creep and manages expectations. For example: "This thesis will focus on X crop in Y region using Z method. It will _not_ cover A, B, or C, though these are noted as directions for future work."
]

== Time Planning

#guide[
  *ABE Guideline:* Indicate what you will realise on specific dates. Try to set dates by which you have answered each research question. Include:

  - Start colloquium date (for MSc thesis)
  - Intended end colloquium date
  - Final thesis assessment date
  - Draft submission dates to supervisor(s)

  A standard MSc thesis (36 ECTS) is equivalent to *25.2 weeks full-time* (approximately 6 months). Account for additional time dedicated to studying for pending exams, vacation, or part-time work. The thesis examination takes place at most 2 months after the initially planned end date — plan the end date carefully.

  *ABE Guideline:* Include a Gantt chart (template available in Brightspace).

  *Tip:* A simple Gantt chart can be built as a Typst table or included as an image. Key phases to show: literature review, data collection, analysis, writing, draft review cycles, and colloquia.
]

